{%- doc -%}
  Somna V2 — wave divider between two colours.

  Figma shapes (shape: 'drip-1' … 'drip-11', 'soft-1', 'soft-2'): the exact wave edges and drops
  traced from the final desktop Figma, drawn as one static SVG (no script). On desktop the full
  1440-wide shape scales with the page; under 750px the middle of the shape is shown larger, as in
  the mobile Figma. Leave `bottom` blank to draw only the top colour and let the wave hang over the
  next section (use with `overlap`).

  shape 'sine' (or blank): the animated "K2" rolling wave drawn by assets/somna-wave.js.

  @param {string} top - colour above the wave
  @param {string} bottom - colour below the wave (blank = transparent, Figma shapes only)
  @param {string} [shape] - wave shape (see above)
  @param {boolean} [overlap] - pull the next section up under the wave (Figma shapes only)
  @param {boolean} [flip] - mirror horizontally
  @param {boolean} [drops] - show the small drops (default true)
  @param {boolean} [animate] - gentle drift, K2 only (default true)
  @param {number} [height] - K2 only: maximum height in px on large screens (default 140)
  @param {number} [height_mobile] - K2 only: minimum height in px on small screens (default 48)
  @param {number} [roll] - K2 only: seconds for one crest to roll past (default 8)
{%- enddoc -%}
